commit b46dccf18ec3f88538851284e385a221453b0864
Author: Christie Hubley <christie@tinkerartstudio.com>
Date:   Sun Sep 27 23:29:37 2026 -0600

    refactor: "Save & mark reviewed" — marking a camp reviewed IS a Save (impl review round 3)
    
    Rounds 1–3 kept finding ways for Mark reviewed to stamp a camp while a grid change on screen hadn't
    saved (a cell typed during the flush, the unsaved flag lost on reopen or overwritten by another camp,
    openStudio text surviving a reopen, the 20 s give-up). Each patch to "flush the auto-save first"
    opened another gap, so the approach is replaced:
    
    - the button is "Save & mark reviewed for <summer>": it runs saveCurriculum({ markReviewed: true }) —
      the normal Save (fields locked, pending auto-save folded in, the WHOLE form written) — and only if
      that save returns true does writeCampReview() stamp reviewedAt/reviewedBy, still inside the lock.
      Save closes the editor as always; the card and count update at once.
    - Undo only clears the stamp (it claims nothing about the form), with the per-opening op token
    - removed: campReviewFlushing, the 20 s timeout, curriculumAutoSaveUnsavedId and its auto-save hooks
    - kept: closeModal refusing to close the editor mid-Save (the generic × handler bypassed that lock)
    - tests rewritten for the flow: save + stamp + count; Undo; Save/rename keep it; typing then
      mark saves both; Save lock (button disabled, no write, can't close); save failure → not reviewed;
      stamp failure after a good save → says so, stays unreviewed; empty name → nothing saved or stamped.
      The card-click helper retries (handlers attach 100 ms after a redraw).
    
    e2e 143/143.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

